From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:32:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 615/615] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini-station: run the eMMC at
 HS200

The station's eMMC still runs at the first boot's conservative 25 MHz
in legacy timing, about 12 MB/s. The vendor runs it at HS400 at
200 MHz. Allow high speed and HS200 at up to 200 MHz on the station:
the eMMC already signals at 1.8 V from VIO18, and mtk-sd tunes HS200
with the MT6797 data it already has. The eMMC's clock mux keeps the
firmware's parent.

HS400 stays out until its data-strobe delay is known.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts  | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index fbd0cb8..b07e1ae 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -671,3 +671,15 @@
 	no-sdio;
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * HS200 on the eMMC, up to 200 MHz on 8 bits with 1.8 V signalling, which
+ * VIO18 already supplies. The vendor runs HS400 from a 400 MHz source;
+ * HS400 needs a data-strobe delay this description doesn't have yet. The
+ * eMMC's clock mux keeps the firmware's parent.
+ */
+&mmc0 {
+	max-frequency = <200000000>;
+	cap-mmc-highspeed;
+	mmc-hs200-1_8v;
+};
